# report/ — the paper and how to rebuild it

`report.pdf` is compiled from `report.tex` (NeurIPS 2026 style `neurips_2026.sty`, submission mode).
Every number in the text is a macro in `numbers.tex`, generated by `make_numbers.py` from the
result files in `results/`; the table (`tables/results_table.tex`) and figure
(`figures/accuracy_fig.pdf`) are generated by the scripts next to them from the same results.

## Rebuild
```
cd report
# 1. analysis (writes results/; see results/README.md and code/)
# 2. figure and table: python3 figures/make_figure.py; python3 tables/make_table.py
python3 make_numbers.py                      # numbers.tex from results/
latexmk -pdf report.tex                      # TeX Live 2026 (pdflatex + bibtex)
```

## Where every number in the text comes from
| In the paper | Macro(s) in `numbers.tex` | Result file and key |
|---|---|---|
| mean accuracy and 95% corrected resampled-t interval, LR / kNN | `\LRmean \LRlo \LRhi`, `\KNNmean \KNNlo \KNNhi` | `results/local/summary.json`: `logistic_regression`, `knn` → `mean`, `corrected.lo/hi` |
| paired difference LR−kNN, interval, p | `\Dmean \Dlo \Dhi \Dp` | same file, `difference_lr_minus_knn` → `mean`, `corrected.*` |
| naive t-interval of the difference (for contrast) | `\Dnaivelo \Dnaivehi` | same, `difference_lr_minus_knn.naive` |
| folds won / lost / tied | `\FoldsLR \FoldsKNN \FoldsTied` | same, `folds_lr_better`, `folds_knn_better`, `folds_tied` |
| k grid, chosen k range and median, grid edge | `\Kgrid \Kmin \Kmax \Kmedian` | same, `protocol.k_grid`, `k_selected_counts`, `k_selected_median`, `k_selected_at_grid_edge` |
| outer seed, LR max_iter, convergence warnings | `\OuterSeed \MaxIter \ConvWarn` | same, `protocol`, `convergence_warnings` |
| Ibex job id, node, CPUs, software versions | `\IbexJob \IbexNode \CPULocal \CPUIbex \Versions` | `results/reproducibility.json`: `ibex_job_id`, `ibex_node`, `env.*` |
| local vs Ibex identical, number of predictions | `\Identical \NPred` | `results/reproducibility.json`: `identical` (+ element-wise flags); `summary.json`: `pooled_correct.of` |
| dataset version, MD5 check | `\DataVersion` | `results/provenance.json` |
| sensitivity variants | `\NVariants \VariantsCoverZero \VariantDmin \VariantDmax` | `results/robustness.json` |

Code producing `results/`: `code/` (experiment-repo). Figure/table generators: `figures/`, `tables/` (figtab-repo).
